/**
\mainpage IP-Glasma Developer Documentation

This is the full developer reference for IP-Glasma: every class, function,
and member variable in `src/`, plus the top-level project documentation
(README, OUTPUT, CONTRIBUTING, CHANGELOG) reproduced as browsable pages
below.
Classes are listed alphabetically (see the "Classes" tab) rather than
grouped by physics topic.

\par Where to start
- \ref md_README -- what IP-Glasma computes, how to build it, and every
  input-file parameter.
- \ref md_OUTPUT -- every output file: when it is written, in which order,
  and its format.
- \ref md_CONTRIBUTING -- coding/documentation conventions for anyone
  changing this codebase.
- \ref md_CHANGELOG -- what changed between versions.

\par The simulation pipeline, in the order a run actually executes it
-# \ref InputFile / \ref Parameters -- read and validate the input file
   (every input parameter is listed once, in ParameterTable.cpp).
-# \ref Glauber -- resolve the nuclear species and their density
   profiles.
-# \ref Init -- build the two nuclei's Wilson lines: \ref NucleusSampler
   samples the nucleon positions, \ref NucleonModel the transverse
   structure of each nucleon (Gaussian, hot spots or strings), \ref NuclearQsTable
   turns the summed thickness into color-charge densities, and the Wilson
   lines are built from the sampled color charges (or read with
   \ref WilsonLineIO, which also writes them).
-# \ref JIMWLK -- (optional) small-\f$x\f$ JIMWLK evolution of the Wilson
   lines before the classical evolution proper.
-# \ref CollisionGeometry -- sample the impact parameter, find the
   wounded nucleons and the overlap-region \f$Q_s\f$, and accept or
   resample the event.
-# \ref ForwardLightCone -- match the two nuclei's fields across the
   forward light cone into the initial gauge links, electric field and
   \f$\pi\f$.
-# \ref Evolution -- leapfrog time evolution of the classical fields, with
   the observables computed from them: \ref EnergyMomentumTensor,
   \ref GluonMultiplicity and \ref Eccentricity.
-# \ref MyEigen -- Landau matching (flow velocity from
   \f$T^{\mu\nu}\f$) and the various binary/text output writers.

\par Supporting/utility classes
- \ref Matrix, \ref Group, \ref SU3.h "SU3" -- the fixed \f$3\times3\f$
  SU(3) matrix type and its generators.
- \ref Lattice, \ref Cell, \ref FFT -- the transverse lattice's field
  storage and Fourier transforms.
- \ref Random -- the pseudorandom-number streams used throughout
  initialization and JIMWLK.
- \ref RunningCoupling.h "RunningCoupling" -- the running \f$\alpha_s\f$
  shared by the collision geometry, the evolution observables and the
  hydro output.
- \ref PhysConst.h "PhysConst" -- physical/mathematical constants shared
  across the codebase.
- \ref PrettyOstream, \ref Instrumentation.h "Instrumentation" --
  logging and profiling.
- \ref GaugeFix, \ref Fragmentation.h "Fragmentation" -- Coulomb gauge
  fixing and KKP hadron fragmentation, both used by
  GluonMultiplicity::compute().

\note CI automatically checks that every class/function/member stays
documented (`.github/workflows/doxygen.yml`), but there is no automated
step that builds and publishes this generated HTML anywhere; see
CONTRIBUTING.md for how to build it locally
(`cmake --build . --target doc`).
*/
